Bit Play
Chefina has a binary string S of **odd** length N. 
She also has an operation string o of length {(N-1)}{2} where o_i \{\&, |, \}. Note that \&, |, denote the bitwise [and](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#AND), [or](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#OR), and [xor](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR) operations respectively.

The following conditions are satisfied with respect to the strings:
- S_3 = S_1 o_1 S_2;
- S_5 = S_3 o_2 S_4;
- S_7 = S_5 o_3 S_6;


- S_N = S_{N-2} o_{ {(N-1)}{2}} S_{N-1}.

Help Chef find the number of operation strings o which satisfy the conditions. Since the number can be huge, print it modulo 10^9+7.

Odd Matrix
You are given an integer N.

Your task is to construct a matrix of size N N satisfying all the following conditions:
- All elements are between 1 and N^2;
- All elements are pairwise **distinct**;
- The sum of elements in every row is **odd**;
- The sum of elements in every column is **odd**.

It can be shown that under the given constraints, at least one such matrix exists for every N. 

If there are multiple answers, you may print any.

Minimum Segments
You are given a string S of length N consisting of lowercase latin alphabets from a to t.

A string is called *good* if the frequency of **all** of the characters present in the string is **odd**. For example, aaba is *good* as there are two characters a and b in the string with frequency 3 and 1 respectively, both of which are odd. The string bcb is not *good* as the frequency of character b is 2.

Find the **minimum** integer k such that there exists an integer array B of size k+1 satisfying:
- B_1 = 0;
- B_{k+1} = N;
- B_i B_{i+1} \ (1 i k);
- S[B_{i}+1, B_{i+1}] is *good* for **all** 1 i k, where S[L, R] denotes the substring S_LS_{L+1} S_R.
